text = "03.04.28
Dear Diary, I had an economics test today. Didn’t go well. At some point, I just stared out of the window. I envy the birds. They get to fly wherever they want to while I’m stuck here. 
You know what? Enough complaining. There’s so much more than grades out there. There are worse problems to deal with.

21.07.28
I went for a run to clear my head. I love running. Mom made me waffles topped with strawberries when I got back.

15.08.28
I heard dad talking to mom earlier, saying some number: 232548
My dad doesn’t talk much, but I know he cares a lot about us. He used to serve time in the military. As much as I’m proud of him for wanting to protect the country, protect us, I wish he didn’t have to fight like that. I don’t know. War traps innocent people in the crossfire. When he came back, he was injured badly, but alive. That’s all mom and I were focused on. I know he lost many comrades, which is probably one of the reasons why he’s so closed off. 

24.08.28
Something about the night sky is just peaceful. I love stargazing. Seeing all the stars reminds me of how there are countless potential endings for a story.


"
autowrap_mode = 2

[node name="Page2" type="Label" parent="CanvasLayer" unique_id=253510597]
